<%= skill %>

Review the changes between `<%= base_ref %>` and `<%= head_ref %>` in this
repository (`git diff <%= base_ref %>...<%= head_ref %>`). The changed files are:
<%- files.each do |file| -%>
- <%= file %>
<%- end -%>

Run the review as the skill describes, then report every finding that
survived your own verification as structured output. Do not post comments,
push, or modify files.

For each finding:
- `file` is the repo-relative path exactly as listed above.
- `affected_lines` use new-side line numbers at `<%= head_ref %>`; only report
  lines added or modified in the diff.
- `severity` and `confidence` use these integer scales (1 is most severe /
  most confident):

Issue severity scale:
<%= severity_scale %>

Confidence scale:
<%= confidence_scale %>

<%= show_threshold_text %>
<%= severity_rubric %>
If you are unsure whether a finding clears the "shown at all" bar above, lean
toward NOT reporting it. If nothing qualifies, return an empty `issues` list.
